.TH BUILDABOOK 1 "October 2026" "buildabook 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.
.SH NAME
buildabook \- build a typeset book from a plain-text outline
.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B buildabook
.I subcommand
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B buildabook spine
.I file.pdf
.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B buildabook
turns a plain-text outline into a typeset book.  One outline file drives the
chapter numbering, the table of contents, and every cross-reference, so the
book is a build artifact of a single source of order.
.PP
The program reads
.IR outline.txt ,
the one source of sequence and numbering, resolves
.B {{token}}
cross-references in the chapter source files, and writes a Typst
.I book.typ
together with a
.I number_map.csv
audit.  It is the build script shared by several book projects, extracted and
written in Ada.
.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B render
Read the outline, resolve tokens, and emit the rendered Typst book and the
number map.  This is the default operation.
.TP
.B check
Validate the outline, the file map, and every token reference.  Emit nothing;
exit nonzero on the first error.
.TP
.B number-map
Write
.I number_map.csv
only.
.TP
.B spine \fIfile.pdf\fR
Rewrite the cover spine width from the page count of
.IR file.pdf ,
updating the
.B #let sw
binding in the cover template.
.TP
.B build
Convenience wrapper: render, compile the PDF with Typst, then run
.BR spine .
.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-outline " file"
Outline file to read (default
.IR outline.txt ).
.TP
.BI \-\-src " dir"
Directory holding the chapter source files (default
.IR chapters ).
.TP
.BI \-\-out " dir"
Directory for the rendered output (default
.IR rendered ).
.TP
.BI \-\-number-map " file"
Where to write the CSV audit (default
.IR number_map.csv ).
.TP
.B \-\-ignore-unmatched
Do not fail when a source file's heading matches no outline token.
.TP
.BI \-\-max-table-rows " n"
Split tables longer than
.I n
rows (0 disables).
.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I outline.txt
The outline: one entry or directive per line, with
.B #
comments.  See
.BR LANGUAGE.md .
.TP
.I filemap.txt
Optional
.IR UUID:filename
map.  When absent, each source file is matched by its first heading.
.TP
.I book.conf
Book metadata (title, author, slug) in the OpenBSD-style configuration
language, parsed by the hbnf runtime.
.TP
.I number_map.csv
Generated audit of every UUID and its rendered designation.
.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TYPST
Path to the Typst compiler, used by
.BR build .
.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero on success; nonzero if the outline, file map, or a token reference is
invalid, or if a subcommand is unknown.
.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
buildabook check
buildabook render --outline outline.txt --src chapters --out rendered
buildabook spine book.pdf
buildabook build
.fi
.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR LANGUAGE.md ,
.BR typst (1)
.
